@startuml animate-stick-figure-class
title animate_stick_figure.py — Class / Module Diagram
left to right direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "scripts/animate_stick_figure.py" {
  class CLI <<module>> {
    +main()
    -parse_args()
    -validate_paths()
  }
  class JSONLLoader <<module>> {
    +load_jsonl(path) : list[Frame]
    -normalize_landmark(item) : Landmark
  }
  class HTMLBuilder <<module>> {
    +make_html(frames, title) : str
    -landmark_map(frame) : dict
    -serialize_frames(frames) : str
  }
  class Frame <<data>> {
    +frame_id : str
    +timestamp_ms : number
    +landmarks : list[Landmark]
  }
  class Landmark <<data>> {
    +index : int
    +x : number
    +y : number
    +visibility : number
  }
}

package "Generated standalone HTML" {
  class PlayerUI <<browser>> {
    +play()
    +pause()
    +restart()
    +seek(timestamp)
    +setSpeed(rate)
  }
  class CanvasRenderer <<browser>> {
    +drawFrame(frame)
    +drawConnections()
  }
  class FrameClock <<browser>> {
    +currentTime() : number
    +nearestFrame(timestamp) : Frame
  }
}

CLI ..> JSONLLoader : loads JSONL
CLI ..> HTMLBuilder : builds HTML
JSONLLoader ..> Frame : creates
Frame "1" *-- "0..33" Landmark : contains
HTMLBuilder ..> Frame : serializes
PlayerUI --> FrameClock : controls timeline
PlayerUI --> CanvasRenderer : requests redraw
FrameClock ..> Frame : selects
CanvasRenderer ..> Frame : draws

note bottom of CLI
Input media/JSONL is read-only.
Output HTML must not overwrite input.
end note
note bottom of PlayerUI
Standalone page; no network requests.
end note
@enduml
